# 19. Payload vs Malware

A payload is not automatically malware.

For example:

```text
Benign Diagnostic Payload
       ↓
Authorized
       ↓
Security Testing
```

versus:

```text
Malicious Payload
       ↓
Unauthorized execution
       ↓
Harm / theft / persistence
```

Intent, functionality, authorization, and context matter.

